Package: anvild
Version: @VERSION@
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Depends: qemu-system-x86, qemu-utils, xorriso, openssh-client, systemd
Recommends: docker.io | docker-ce
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Maintainer: filippo ferrando <ferrandodfilippo@ik.me>
Homepage: https://git.fferrando.cc/rdfilippo/anvil
Description: Daemon for anvil - manages QEMU VMs and Docker/Podman containers
 anvild is the daemon anvil (the CLI/TUI) talks to over a unix socket. It
 drives qemu-system-x86_64 processes directly (no libvirt) for VMs, and
 Docker (Podman support planned) for containers.
 .
 Runs as an unprivileged "anvil" system user, created automatically on
 install (see postinst). Not started automatically; enable it yourself
 with systemctl enable --now anvild once installed.
